caption: The Blood Moon
setting-component: the-blood-moon

The Blood Moon occurs on the night of the new moon. The Hunt begins at sunset and ends at dawn.

During that period, qualifying deaths performed according to Niktul’s rules count as sacrifices to him under Godmath. A qualifying victim’s higher soul is claimed by Niktul and sent to his torment afterlife. The sacrifice therefore does more than kill the victim: it condemns the sacrificed soul to Niktul’s Hell, where it can be tormented as a continuing source of divine power.
